 "text": "Hey, how are you doing right now? Find a dry and stable spot in the tent and stay there. Light and heavy rain are pretty much the big ones, wind and lightning are what you really need to worry about. If you' sure the storm is past, then do a quick check of tent before you go out. Check all the pegs and guy ropes are secure. No, only in an emergency. Pack up in the morning, when you' ready to leave. The tent is made to be set up and torn down several times. Find a large rock or a big tree, and stay there. Lightening often strikes where you' hiking, so choosing a spot with a bit of height actually increases your risk.",
